But you — having seen the fulfilment, the complete consummation of desire (for here all desires are completely fulfilled); the foundation, the support of the world consisting of the adhyātma, adhibhūta and adhidaiva, since it is the Self of all; the fruit of upāsanā (meditative worship), namely the station of Hiraṇyagarbha; endlessness, that is, infinity; and the further shore, the supreme limit of fearlessness;

the stoma, that which is praiseworthy, the great, conjoined with manifold qualities such as the lordly powers beginning with aṇimā — and being both stoma and mahat together, since it is unsurpassed, it is called stoma-mahat; the urugāya, the wide-extending course; the pratiṣṭhā, the supreme station of the self, than which there is none higher;

having beheld all this, by firmness, by steadfastness, you, Naciketas, who are dhīra — endowed with intelligence and discrimination — atyasrākṣīḥ, that is, longing only for the highest, you have cast aside this whole accumulation of saṃsāric enjoyment. Ah, indeed you are of unsurpassed excellence!

Mṛtyu, having been thus questioned, spoke, intending to declare both the thing asked and a further specification. All the Vedas — that station (pada) which is to be reached, to be attained — proclaim without division, without contradiction, that is, expound; and all austerities, of which the meaning is that they are undertaken for the attainment of that;

desiring which men practise brahmacarya — characterised by residence in the teacher's house, or any other discipline undertaken for the attainment of Brahman — that station, the very thing you wish to know, I tell you in brief, in summary: it is Om.

That very station which is sought to be known by you — that very same is denoted by the syllable Om and has Om as its symbol (pratīka).

ഇപ്രകാരം ചോദിച്ച നചികേതസ്സിനോട് മൃത്യു ചോദിച്ച വസ്തുവിനെയും ഒരു വിശേഷണാന്തരത്തെയും വിവക്ഷിച്ച് പറഞ്ഞു. സകല വേദങ്ങളും ഏതു പദത്തെ — പദനീയമായതിനെ, ഗമനീയമായതിനെ — അവിഭാഗേന, അവിരോധേന, ആമനനം ചെയ്യുന്നുവോ, പ്രതിപാദിക്കുന്നുവോ; സകല തപസ്സുകളും ഏതിനെ പറയുന്നുവോ — ഏതിന്റെ പ്രാപ്ത്യര്‍ത്ഥമായവ എന്നര്‍ത്ഥം;

ഏതിനെ ഇച്ഛിച്ച് ഗുരുകുലവാസലക്ഷണമോ മറ്റോ ആയ ബ്രഹ്മചര്യത്തെ — ബ്രഹ്മപ്രാപ്ത്യര്‍ത്ഥമായി — ആചരിക്കുന്നുവോ, ആ പദത്തെ — നീ അറിയാന്‍ ഇച്ഛിക്കുന്നതിനെ — ഞാന്‍ നിനക്ക് സംഗ്രഹേണ, സംക്ഷേപേണ, പറയുന്നു: അത് 'ഓം' എന്നതുതന്നെ.

നീ അറിയാന്‍ ഇച്ഛിച്ച ഈ പദം ഏതോ, അത് ഈ 'ഓം' എന്ന ശബ്ദത്താല്‍ വാച്യവും ഓംശബ്ദപ്രതീകവുമാകുന്നു.
